WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.862
Coding Exercise 3 asks you to insert a specific row
and verify

00:00:03.888 --> 00:00:07.738
it with RETURNING You need to add Maya Brooks with
MRN one

00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:12.988
zero one two age thirty-one and gender Female The
INSERT statement already

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:17.638
lists the target columns Your job is to complete the
VALUES section

00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:21.462
The four values must appear in the same order as the
columns

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:27.100
MRN full name age and gender Remember that text
values need single

00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:32.737
quotes The numeric age does not need quotes After
the VALUES section

00:00:32.962 --> 00:00:36.800
keep the RETURNING clause so PostgreSQL displays the
row that was inserted

00:00:37.688 --> 00:00:42.238
Before running the statement count the columns and
count the values There

00:00:42.262 --> 00:00:45.688
should be four of each Then read the row back from
left

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.650
to right and make sure each value belongs to the
correct column

00:00:49.538 --> 00:00:53.900
Click Run and Check If the statement succeeds look
at the returned

00:00:53.925 --> 00:00:58.725
MRN name age and gender If you get a unique
constraint error

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.588
check whether you already inserted the same MRN
during an earlier attempt

00:01:03.475 --> 00:01:08.638
You can reset the exercise environment if
appropriate The important habit here

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:14.250
is not just INSERT It is insert and verify RETURNING
gives you

00:01:14.275 --> 00:01:16.250
immediate evidence of what was stored
